// m0900 — DJI Phantom 3 Professional air-side MCU (STM32F103) platform for Renode.
//
// Extends Renode's stock STM32F103 description (which models the core, flash, SRAM,
// USARTs, timers, GPIO, DMA and NVIC) and adds the two SPI controllers the firmware uses
// plus an AD9363 SPI tap on each, so the runtime-computed RF config can be captured.
//
// Firmware facts (docs/renode-task.md / docs/cpu-reversing-proof.md):
//   app base   0x08008000   (bootloader occupies 0x08000000..0x08008000)
//   initial SP 0x20004cb8
//   reset vec  0x08008201
// The stock description maps flash at 0x00000000 size 0x20000000, which backs 0x08008000,
// and SRAM at 0x20000000. The reset SP/PC are taken from the firmware's own vector table
// once VectorTableOffset is set to 0x08008000 (done in the .resc).

using "platforms/cpus/stm32f103.repl"

// SPI1 and SPI2 are both referenced by m0900; one of them is the AD9363 control bus
// (docs/control-plane-re.md). NVIC positions: SPI1 = 35, SPI2 = 36 on STM32F103.
spi1: SPI.STM32SPI @ sysbus 0x40013000
    series: STM32Series.F1
    IRQ -> nvic@35

spi2: SPI.STM32SPI @ sysbus 0x40003800
    series: STM32Series.F1
    IRQ -> nvic@36

// AD9363 transceiver, tapped on BOTH candidate buses. Whichever SPI the firmware actually
// drives will accumulate transactions; the other stays empty. This empirically settles the
// open "confirm which SPI drives the AD9363" question from the task spec. AD9363SpiTap is
// an external peripheral compiled from renode/peripherals/AD9363SpiTap.cs — the .resc must
// `include` it before loading this platform.
ad9363_spi1: SPI.AD9363SpiTap @ spi1

ad9363_spi2: SPI.AD9363SpiTap @ spi2

// RCC isn't modeled (same gap the stock repl's own RCC_CR tag works around), so CFGR's
// SWS bits never report "switched to PLL" and the firmware's clock-switch wait spins
// forever. Statically tag it with SWS=PLL (bits[3:2]=10) pre-set, same pattern as the
// stock RCC_CR tag below it. Verified: without this, boot never reaches the AD9363
// bring-up (confirmed by running the real m0900 firmware - see docs/phy-params.md).
sysbus:
    init:
        Tag <0x40021004, 0x40021007> "RCC_CFGR" 0x00000008
